From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mt76 review <mt76@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: check the length of a radar report

mt7915_mcu_rx_radar_detected() reads rdd_idx, at offset 36, from an
event whose length comes straight from the DMA descriptor.  Drop a
report too short to hold it.

The other checks of the original patch (response header, EFUSE_ACCESS
length and valid flag, GET_MIB_INFO length, unwritten efuse blocks in
mt7915_eeprom_load()) are in mt76 upstream as of 2026-10-28.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992@localhost>
---
--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -318,6 +318,10 @@
 	struct mt7915_mcu_rdd_report *r;
 	u32 sku;
 
+	/* only rdd_idx is read here; the pulse arrays are not used */
+	if (skb->len < offsetof(struct mt7915_mcu_rdd_report, rdd_idx) + 1)
+		return;
+
 	r = (struct mt7915_mcu_rdd_report *)skb->data;
 
 	switch (r->rdd_idx) {
